sequenceDiagram
    participant C as Client
    participant S as TCP / HTTP endpoint
    participant M as MultiRaftStore
    participant L as Group leader
    participant F as Follower replicas
    participant SM as State machine (RedisStore)

    C->>S: SET key value  /  PUT /api/keys/key
    S->>M: authenticate, then set(key, value)
    Note over M: groupFor(key) selects the owning group<br/>on the virtual-node hash ring
    M->>L: propose write to the owning group (a follower forwards it to the leader over peer RPC)
    activate L
    Note over L: append entry to the durable Raft log
    L->>F: AppendEntries over mutual-TLS RPC
    F-->>L: acknowledged by a majority
    Note over L: advance commit index
    L->>SM: apply committed entry (WAL or RocksDB write)
    deactivate L
    L-->>M: committed
    M-->>S: OK
    S-->>C: +OK  /  200 saved

    Note over C,SM: Reads go through ReadIndex on the leader. With KV_FOLLOWER_READS=true, a follower may serve reads while within KV_FOLLOWER_MAX_COMMIT_LAG.
